    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d893">

                <pb facs="1069" n="1059" xml:id="pg1059"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.515/567a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-17T23:00:00-04:00">March 17, 1943—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>477. For Murphy:<anchor n="11" xml:id="d893-f1"/> The Treasury has proposed to
                    the Finance Ministers of the United Nations and associated American governments
                    the sending of an expert to Washington to enter into informal and tentative
                    explorations of possible plans for monetary stabilization in the post-war
                    period.</p>
                <p>You are requested to make this known to General Giraud<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d893-f2"/> and to General Catroux<anchor n="13" xml:id="d893-f3"/>
                    and to inquire whether they could agree on such an expert who might assist in
                    such exploratory discussions on the technical level by giving a French reaction
                    to the suggestions discussed. Both the Treasury and the Department would hope
                    that they would speak with one voice, so that we are not in the position of
                    having the appearance of two interests, instead of one.</p>
                <p>Cooperation between the two groups would be welcomed as a sign of increasing
                    progress towards unity.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d893-f1" n="11" xml:id="d893-f1-content">
                <p>Robert D. Murphy, U.S. Political Adviser, staff of the Supreme Allied Commander,
                    Mediterranean Theatre; Personal Representative of the President in North Africa
                    with rank of Minister.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d893-f2" n="12" xml:id="d893-f2-content">
                <p>Gen. Henri Honoré Giraud, French High Commissioner in North Africa from December
                    26, 1942.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d893-f3" n="13" xml:id="d893-f3-content">
                <p>Gen. Georges Catroux, member of the Council of Defence of the French Empire, of
                    which Gen. Charles de Gaulle was president.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
